Q1. What is JUnit?

Interview Ready Answer

JUnit is an open-source Java testing framework used to write and
execute Unit Tests.

It helps developers automatically verify that individual methods or
classes work correctly by executing test cases.

Key Points

• Open-source Java testing framework.
• Used for Unit Testing.
• Automates test execution.
• Supports Test-Driven Development (TDD).
• Displays test results as PASS or FAIL.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need JUnit?

Interview Ready Answer

JUnit is used to automate Unit Testing, detect bugs early, reduce
manual testing effort, and improve software quality.

It also provides confidence that code changes do not break existing
functionality.

Advantages

• Automates testing.
• Detects bugs early.
• Saves development time.
• Supports TDD.
• Simplifies regression testing.
• Improves software quality.

Real-Life Example

Calculator

Expected

2 + 3 = 5

↓

JUnit automatically executes the test.

↓

PASS or FAIL is displayed.

Instead of checking the result manually.

======================================================================

Q3. What is the purpose of @Test annotation?

Interview Ready Answer

@Test is a JUnit annotation used to mark a method as a test case.

JUnit executes only those methods that are annotated with @Test.

Important

Without @Test,

JUnit does NOT recognize the method as a test case.

======================================================================

Q4. What are Assertions in JUnit?

Interview Ready Answer

Assertions are methods used to verify whether the actual output
matches the expected output.

If both values are equal, the test passes.
Otherwise, the test fails.

Most Common Assertion

assertEquals(expected, actual)

Purpose

Compares the expected result with the actual result.

======================================================================

Q5. What is the Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) Pattern?

Interview Ready Answer

The Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) Pattern is a standard structure for
writing Unit Test cases.

Arrange

Prepare objects and test data.

↓

Act

Execute the method under test.

↓

Assert

Verify the result using assertions.

Benefits

• Improves readability.
• Makes test cases easy to understand.
• Provides a standard testing structure.

======================================================================

Q6. What are @BeforeEach and @AfterEach?

Interview Ready Answer

@BeforeEach

Runs before every test case.

Used to initialize objects, resources, or test data required for the
test.

------------------------------------------------------------

@AfterEach

Runs after every test case.

Used to clean up resources or reset the test environment after the
test finishes.

